# Wildwood Mentor {2}{G} (1/1): "Whenever a token you control enters, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature" (CR 603.2, 111.1) and
# "Whenever this creature attacks, another target attacking creature gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is this creature's power".
# Turn 1: Bot1 casts Wildwood Mentor (Black Lotus) and an Alpine Grizzly (three Moxen). Turn 2: Bot2's Dragon Fodder makes two Goblin
# tokens under Bot2's control: no counter for Bot1's Mentor. Turn 3: Bot1's own Dragon Fodder makes two Goblins: two triggers, the
# Mentor becomes 3/3 (the Goblins, summoning sick, stay home). Both attack: the Mentor's trigger gives the Grizzly +3/+3 (X is the
# power on resolution), 7/5. 20 - 3 - 7 = 10. Turn 5: the Mentor attacks alone, so there is no other attacker to target: no pump, and
# it just deals its 3.

